_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 25
---
order: 25
---
short_label: X.25
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: The rectangle contained by medial straight lines commensurable in square only is either rational or medial.
----
proof:

Let the rectangle {AC|ACh} be contained by the medial straight lines {AB} and {BC} which are commensurable in square only.

I say that {AC|ACh} is either rational or medial.

Describe the squares {AD|ADh} and {BE|BEh} on {AB} and {BC}. Then each of the squares {AD|ADh} and {BE|BEh} is medial.

Set out a rational straight line {FG}. Apply the rectangular parallelogram {GH|GHh} to {FG} equal to {AD|ADh}, producing {FH} as breadth, apply the rectangular parallelogram {MK|MKh} to {HM} equal to {AC|ACh}, producing {HK} as breadth, and further apply similarly {NL|NLh} to {KN} equal to {BE|BEh}, producing {KL} as breadth. Then {FH}, {HK}, and {KL} are in a straight line.

Since each of the squares {AD|ADh} and {BE|BEh} is medial, and {AD|ADh} equals {GH|GHh} while {BE|BEh} equals {NL|NLh}, therefore each of the rectangles {GH|GHh} and {NL|NLh} is also medial.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="340" height="270" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.25 diagram" src="propX25.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
