</figure>

And they are applied to the rational straight line {FG}, therefore each of the straight lines {FH} and {KL} is rational and incommensurable in length with {FG}. [!just X.22]

And, since {AD|ADh} is commensurable with {BE|BEh}, therefore {GH|GHh} is commensurable with {NL|NLh}. And {GH|GHh} is to {NL|NLh} as {FH} is to {KL}, therefore {FH} is commensurable in length with {KL}. [!just VI.1; X.11]

Therefore {FH} and {KL} are rational straight lines commensurable in length, therefore the rectangle {FH} by {KL} is rational. [!just X.19]

And, since {DB} equals {BA|AB} while {OB|BO} equals {BC}, therefore {DB} is to {BC} as {AB} is to {BO}.

But {DB} is to {BC} as {DA|ADh} is to {AC|ACh}, and {AB} is to {BO} as {AC|ACh} is to {CO|BEh}, therefore {DA|ADh} is to {AC|ACh} as {AC|ACh} is to {CO|BEh}. [!just VI.1]

But {AD|ADh} equals {GH|GHh}, {AC|ACh} equals {MK|MKh}, and {CO|BEh} equals {NL|NLh}, therefore {GH|GHh} is to {MK|MKh} as {MK|MKh} is to {NL|NLh}. Therefore {FH} is to {HK} as {HK} is to {KL}. Therefore the rectangle {FH} by {KL} equals the square on {HK}. [!just VI.1, V.11; VI.17]

But the rectangle {FH} by {KL} is rational, therefore the square on {HK} is also rational.

Therefore {HK} is rational. And, if it is commensurable in length with {FG}, then {HN|MKh} is rational, but, if it is incommensurable in length with {FG}, then {KH|HK} and {HM} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only, and therefore {HN|MKh} is medial. [!just X.19; X.21]

Therefore {HN|MKh} is either rational or medial. But {HN|MKh} equals {AC|ACh}, therefore {AC|ACh} is either rational or medial.

Therefore, *the rectangle contained by medial straight lines commensurable in square only is either rational or medial.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide:

To say a rectangle with sides *a* and *b* is rational says that *ab* is a rational number. To say that it's medial says that (*ab*)² is a rational number but *ab* is an irrational number. Therefore, to say it is either rational or medial says only that (*ab*)² is a rational number.

In this proposition we are given that *a* and *b* are medial, so both *a*⁴ and *b*⁴ are rational numbers, and we are given that *a*²/*b*² is a rational number. Therefore, (*ab*)², which equals *b*⁴(*a*²/*b*²) is also a rational number.

This proposition is not used in the rest of the *Elements*.
